{"Title":"An Act to establish the Massachusetts National Guard Museum in Salem","BillNumber":"H3492","DocketNumber":"HD4014","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"M_C3","Name":"Manny Cruz","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C3","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:33:53.317"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"M_C3","Name":"Manny Cruz","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C3","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:33:53.3166667"},{"Id":"JAP1","Name":"Jerald A. Parisella","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:07:01.1066667"},{"Id":"AJS1","Name":"Adam J. Scanlon","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-23T10:55:18.7733333"},{"Id":"SSH1","Name":"Steven S. Howitt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SSH1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T07:34:54.18"},{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-06-30T15:24:52.3366667"},{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-10-18T16:43:24.99"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"JAP1","Name":"Jerald A. Parisella","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:06:14.247"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3492/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives Cruz of Salem and Parisella of Beverly, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3492) of Manny Cruz, Jerald A. Parisella and others for legislation to establish the Massachusetts National Guard Museum in the city of Salem.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\t     Chapter 33 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting, after section 139, the following section:-\r\n\t              Section 140. There shall be a permanent museum for the Massachusetts National Guard located in the City of Salem as the federal birthplace of the National Guard. Furthermore, it shall be recognized as the official military museum for the commonwealth of Massachusetts. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}